LRC14 binding-pair switch carrier scout
========================================================================
Assumption challenge
  Candidate vertex sets considered:
    runners, gaps, fixed sections, section boundaries, wall crossings,
    residues, cover arcs, Fourier modes, matroid circuits, proof obligations,
    and binding-pair switches.
  Chosen vertex set:
    binding-pair/proof switches, because THM-524 says the max is there but
    the LRC predicate is only preserved after the other-runner clearance scan.
  Preserved predicate:
    existence of a time with min_v ||v t|| >= 1/14.
  Destroyed by raw pair quotients:
    active blocker deck, endpoint owners, off-grid witness intervals, and
    whether the promising pair is blocked by another runner.

