[3] Tournament Analysis
  vertices are switch/proof carriers, not runners.
  pairwise observable:
    predicate retention, clearance retention, exact denominator scale,
    off-grid coverage, family separation, decoy resistance, proof maturity.
  binary gauge:
    carrier A -> B when A wins a majority of observable coordinates; ties
    use the declared Hamiltonian path below.
  score_hist=[(0, 1), (1, 1), (2, 1), (3, 1), (5, 3), (7, 1), (8, 1)]
  directed_3cycles=1
  scc_sizes=[3, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
  hamiltonian_path_count=3
  tie_hamiltonian_path=others_clear_binding_switch > covering_big_flank_switch > grid_section_unit_witness > binding_denominator_lane > active_blocker_deck > complement_sum14_boundary > state_lift_nonunit_pair > raw_pair_gap_shadow > snapshot_position_tournament

[4] Proof-angle target
  Add binding-switch fields to HYP-2963-style packet records:
    binding_switch_type, active_pair_shell, denominator_lane,
    active_blocker_deck, other_clearance_margin, decoy_pair_gap,
    grid_or_offgrid_status, and switch_witness_count.
  The theorem-facing lemma is not 'large pair gap implies LRC witness'.
  It is the stronger switch statement:
    a quotient may keep a binding pair only when the active blocker deck and
    all other-runner clearance inequalities are retained, reconstructed,
    dual-annihilated, or routed to AP/GW, covering, petal, K33, or F7 debt.
